you're doing this one step

792
00:42:36,820 --> 00:42:39,810
temporal difference
between the reward

793
00:42:39,810 --> 00:42:43,133
plus the value here, minus the
value at the current state.

794
00:42:43,133 --> 00:42:45,050
And so one alternative
thing that you could do

795
00:42:45,050 --> 00:42:52,050
is, instead of using
this estimated--

796
00:42:52,050 --> 00:42:56,730
this reward plus value, which
is basically the estimated

797
00:42:56,730 --> 00:42:59,890
future rewards, if
you start at state t

798
00:42:59,890 --> 00:43:05,990
and take action a minus
your current value is,

799
00:43:05,990 --> 00:43:12,010
instead, you could simply use
the empirical sum of rewards

800
00:43:12,010 --> 00:43:14,050
into the future.

801
00:43:14,050 --> 00:43:17,590
And so this could
simply be the--

802
00:43:17,590 --> 00:43:30,530

803
00:43:30,530 --> 00:43:33,210
and this is going to
be a little bit simpler

804
00:43:33,210 --> 00:43:38,770
and doesn't rely on having
a good temporal difference

805
00:43:38,770 --> 00:43:41,130
between the two.

806
00:43:41,130 --> 00:43:43,490
And so, specifically,
we can first

807
00:43:43,490 --> 00:43:45,882
estimate the value
function by trying

808
00:43:45,882 --> 00:43:48,090
to minimize the difference
between our value estimate

809
00:43:48,090 --> 00:43:49,970
and the sum of rewards.

810
00:43:49,970 --> 00:43:53,550
And then to estimate
the advantage function,

811
00:43:53,550 --> 00:43:59,050
