813
00:44:02,330 --> 00:44:07,290
In terms of this
particular advantage

814
00:44:07,290 --> 00:44:11,930
estimate corresponds to a
fairly simple and fairly popular

815
00:44:11,930 --> 00:44:14,190
algorithm called advantage
weighted regression.

816
00:44:14,190 --> 00:44:18,610

817
00:44:18,610 --> 00:44:24,690
And I should emphasize that the
way that we did it, previously,

818
00:44:24,690 --> 00:44:29,090
where you used r plus V of
s t plus 1 is also valid.

819
00:44:29,090 --> 00:44:30,730
This simply
corresponds to a method

820
00:44:30,730 --> 00:44:33,330
that is used pretty
commonly, and seems

821
00:44:33,330 --> 00:44:37,440
to work well in practice, when
you have an offline data set.

822
00:44:37,440 --> 00:44:39,800
The question was we
talked about before,

823
00:44:39,800 --> 00:44:42,840
how this is somewhat high
variance, and GAE is better.

824
00:44:42,840 --> 00:44:46,080
You could also use
GAE here, definitely.

825
00:44:46,080 --> 00:44:49,320
This is going to be
a little bit simpler.

826
00:44:49,320 --> 00:44:53,720
But yeah, you could also use
generalized advantage estimation

827
00:44:53,720 --> 00:44:54,532
here.

828
00:44:54,532 --> 00:44:55,740
Yeah, that's a good question.

829
00:44:55,740 --> 00:44:59,340
So the question is, are we
bringing up this Monte Carlo

830
00:44:59,340 --> 00:45:01,800
because, with
offline data set, we

831
00:45:01,800 --> 00:45:04,380
have enough data that sum
of rewards is more accurate,

