922
00:49:30,500 --> 00:49:33,860
OK, so the full algorithm is,
we first fit a value function,

923
00:49:33,860 --> 00:49:36,500
using Monte Carlo regression.

924
00:49:36,500 --> 00:49:41,700
And then we train
a policy, where

925
00:49:41,700 --> 00:49:44,900
we weight the
probability of picking

926
00:49:44,900 --> 00:49:47,420
an action or the
likelihood objective

927
00:49:47,420 --> 00:49:51,500
by the exponentiated advantage
estimate, where the advantage

928
00:49:51,500 --> 00:49:55,140
estimate is given by the sum
of rewards minus the value

929
00:49:55,140 --> 00:49:56,140
function.

930
00:49:56,140 --> 00:49:58,660
And we have this
hyperparameter here

931
00:49:58,660 --> 00:50:05,020
that controls the temperature,
or how spiky this distribution

932
00:50:05,020 --> 00:50:05,580
will be.

933
00:50:05,580 --> 00:50:10,220
One of the upsides of this
algorithm is very, very simple.

934
00:50:10,220 --> 00:50:12,620
It's like, yeah, probably
the simplest thing

935
00:50:12,620 --> 00:50:14,140
that you could
implement that has

936
00:50:14,140 --> 00:50:19,300
the possibility of improving
over filtered imitation

